// test::dir is the directory of the running test's own file, as an absolute path: a test
// reads a file kept beside it wherever `ctxc test` is run from. It is the test's, also in
// a fn of another file that the test calls (lib/beside.ctx), and each directory of the
// program has its own: the root's, and one that `build::add_sources` adds. A generated
// file's test is given the directory ctxc wrote the file in. Each test here passes its
// first check, of the file's text, and fails the second to show its directory.
//# $ ctxc test .
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| app/main_test.ctx:5: fail: beside_the_root: test::dir{ &t } == "?": {dir}/app == ?
//| lib/deep/more_test.ctx:6: fail: deep::in_an_added_directory: test::dir{ &t } == "?": {dir}/lib/deep == ?
//| {work:.}/gen/app/made.ctx:2: fail: in_a_generated_file: test::dir{ &t } == "?": {work:.}/gen/app == ?
//| tests: 3 run, 0 passed, 3 failed, 0 skipped, 0 not selected, 5 checks

// From another working directory the files are named from there, and the directories are
// the same.
//# $ ctxc test .. beside deep
//# cwd: elsewhere
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| ../app/main_test.ctx:5: fail: beside_the_root: test::dir{ &t } == "?": {dir}/app == ?
//| ../lib/deep/more_test.ctx:6: fail: deep::in_an_added_directory: test::dir{ &t } == "?": {dir}/lib/deep == ?
//| tests: 2 run, 0 passed, 2 failed, 0 skipped, 1 not selected, 4 checks
